  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>RCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Br</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mtext>&#160;Acetone&#160;</mtext></mover><munder><mrow><msub><mi>RCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mtext>&#160;major&#160;</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>Br</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></p><p>The correct statement is</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Br</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;can act as competing nucleophile.</p>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<p>The reaction can occur in acetic acid also.</p>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<p>The transition state formed in the above&nbsp;reaction is less polar than the localised anion.</p>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<p>The solvent used in the reaction solvates the&nbsp;ions formed in rate determining step</p>",
      "is_correct": false
